~ start
Max: Can’t you guys believe it’s Christmas already? A full year of working as bonafide adults in the photography industry.
Joshua: Oh shut up. Us? Adults? We just graduated from highschool yesterday, what do you mean?
Martin: Yeah, it was just last week when Nugget was trying to eat Max’s cafeteria lunch.
Max: *chuckle* That takes me back. I miss that stupid little cat in that stupid little highschool.
Martin: And he misses your lunches too. 
Joshua: Aren’t you going back to the province tomorrow, Max?
Max: I’m dreading the commute back though. Jam-packed in a bus like a can of sardines in the midst of Christmas traffic? I’m already sweating just thinking about it.
Joshua: I mean that’s practically expected already. Every commute here in the Philippines is like going through the 9 circles of hell.
Max: I guess so.
Martin: You got your pasalubong already? Surely you don’t plan on going back home empty-handed.
Max: Oh shoot, you’re right. I’m gonna have to think about it on the way home. Thanks for the reminder.
do play_doorbell()
Driver: BabaMove delivery for Max Bayubay?
Joshua: That’s your cue.
Max: For me? I don’t think I got anything delivered.
=> END